{"name":"Pedigree","hex":"#31646e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pedigree","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A chart, list, or record of ancestors, to show breeding, especially distinguished breeding. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A person's ancestral history; ancestry, lineage."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pedigree.","Purebred."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pedigree"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pedigree chart","blocks":[{"text":"A pedigree chart is a diagram that shows the occurrence of certain traits through different generations of a family, most commonly for humans and animal breed registration."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/XBio_illustration_%E2%80%93_Pedigree.png/330px-XBio_illustration_%E2%80%93_Pedigree.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pedigree_chart","wikidata":"Q3242583"},{"title":"Genealogy","blocks":[{"text":"Genealogy is the study of families, family history, and the tracing of their lineages. Genealogists use oral interviews, historical records, genetic analysis, and other records to obtain information about a family and to demonstrate kinship and pedigrees of its members. The results are often displayed in charts or written as narratives. The field of family history is broader than genealogy, and covers not just lineage but also family and community history and biography."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/900-158_Ahnentafel_Herzog_Ludwig.jpg/330px-900-158_Ahnentafel_Herzog_Ludwig.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genealogy","wikidata":"Q47307"},{"title":"Pedigree (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Pedigree  is an autobiographical novel by the Belgian author Georges Simenon, first published in 1948. Simenon described the work as \"a book in which 